<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomon Gafabusa Iguru I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Gafabusa Iguru I is the omukama of Bunyoro-Kitara, crowned in 1994 after the monarchy was restored as a cultural institution without governmental powers. He is a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tito-winyi-iv">Tito Winyi IV</a>. His role is ceremonial and cultural, but the kingdom has spoken on land and on oil discovered around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-albert">Lake Albert</a>.</p></div>
